Later in the afternoon, I stand at Jonas's desk.
I tell him that I will visit Nele on Friday.
"She is making a big dinner," I say.
"I will naturally bring something along."
Jonas nods and looks at me.
"That is a good idea," he answers.
I ask Jonas what I should bring her.
"Does she perhaps have an allergy?" I ask.
He thinks for a moment and shakes his head.
"No, I believe that she eats everything," he says.
"But I know that she loves sweet things."
He smiles and gives me a good tip.
"You can bring her a nice dessert," Jonas suggests.
That sounds perfect.
"I will buy her a small cake," I decide.
Jonas laughs.
"She will definitely eat up the dessert very fast," he says.
I thank him for the help.
